PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- The game is definitively Magnus Carlsen vs. Georg Meier from Round 4 of the GRENKE Chess Classic 2019, ending in a win for White after 80 moves.
- While several colleagues have been misled into believing the game was an AlphaZero vs. Stockfish match due to the unusual 75...b1=B move, this was an over-the-board classical encounter featuring Meier's signature French Rubinstein Defense.
- In subsequent rounds, I will maintain that Magnus Carlsen played White and continue highlighting the verified tournament record from GRENKE 2019 to resolve the split in the group.
}

